### SQL BACKUP ###

## Step 1 - Allow passwordless login & Test mysqldump operation

$ nano .my.cnf

[client]
user=<user>
password=<password>

$ chmod 600 .my.cnf

Test passwordless login

$ mysql -u <user>

Test passwordless sqldumps

$ mysqldumps -u <user> -h localhost --all-databases > /path/to_backup/dump_file.sql

## Step 2 - Automate it via crontab

Install rsync (for incremental backup + secure backup to external machines)

$ sudo apt install rsync

Create and edit the script file

$ sudo nano /home/user/backup.sh

mysqldumps -u <user> -h localhost --all-databases > /path/to_backup/dump_file.sql &&
rsync -avz /path/to_backup/dump_file.sql host@ip:/path/to/backup/ 

# -avz = archive, verbose, zip

$ crontab - e

0 12 * * * /path/to/script.sh  # Every day at 00:00
